{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980165-\u200b-2e-fight-fire-with-fire-running-awakened-antagonists","id":980165,"title":"\u200b[2E] Fight Fire With Fire - Running Awakened Antagonists","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-02T02:27:19-07:00","id":980165,"title":"\u200b[2E] Fight Fire With Fire - Running Awakened Antagonists","content":"<br /> So my long players are a bit dissatisfied how I run Awakened antagonists, combat scene especially. They do not feel \u2018challenge\u2019 in my magical fight scenes. It\u2019s probably with way how I\u2019m the only Mage Storyteller in city ( or I know about ) and by this I have low experience on playing Awakened characters themselves, particularly on focusing on sole Arcana effects. So I\u2019m asking to help me learn better system and show \u2018how Mage pros do this\u2019. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Basically, what would you cast as example NPC characters in combat on my place as player.<br /> <br /> To not be unfounded, here is Scelesti cabal I want to put my players against on next session. Attack on them is done with 10 Pentacle mages ( including 4 PCs ) and they are so much pressed to wall, they <i>want</i> to summon and control their Paradox Reaches to their advantage on battle filed. Including summoning Rank 5 Abyssal Entity they worship. Each one of them is member of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/25143-children-of-the-stars-aliens-loving-legacy\">Children of Stars</a> Legacy and it\u2019s coven in Greenwich Observatory. ( Of course, feel free to steal those to your games in London. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <b>Precession</b> - Acanthus of Free Council, leader of the coven and 40-something female astronomer by day and New Age astrologer by night. She was raised as white British in London, but went to New York for studies, were she was inducted in to Legacy. She left NYC community for few years, going around few Consilia, always a bit out of place. Until she return to London in 2002, to take over her post in the Observatory and started Children\u2019s coven here \u2013 members joined in few next years, with last local \u2013 <b>Iphis</b> - added in 2011. Rather reasonable demeanor, but truly fixated on the \u201ccosmic\u201d aspect of the Legacy. She was convinced by the rest to dwell in to Yellow Sign phenomena as scientific/magical experiment to prove.<br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> 7<br /> <b>Arcana:</b> Fate 4, Life 2, Prime 5, Space 2, Time 4<br /> <br /> <b>Hastur</b> - Mastigos of Free Council, 30-something British male s-f horror writer, the UFO conspiracy theorist in reality. He said he was \u201ctaken\u201d at age of 19 and from them on he tries to remember all the details of his abduction, in way to solve how to be with aliens once more \u2013 in reality, it was his Awakening. He sees Children of the Stars on quasi spiritual level, trying to piece the elements need for the Second Contact. He thinks the Yellow Sign is a way to bring Them here, to commune with rest of Children \u2013 and so he choose name Hastur \u2013 from the being that \u201cabducted\u201d him in his Awakening.<br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> 5<br /> <b>Arcana:</b> Mind 4, Prime 3, Space 4, Time 4<br /> <br /> <b>Patterson</b> - Obrimos of Free Council, 30-something black female archaeologist, Libertine archeomancer. When she was Sleeper, she was making her studies on Temples of Time Before and she discovered that dating is impossible \u2013 and Awaken by this fact. Joined Children because she ferociously disapproves Atlantis Myth, seeing there is more to the Truth. She choose Shadow Name from Clair Cameron Patterson, a scientist who produced one of the most accurate measures of the age of the Earth, however he had a lot of trouble calculating this due to human pollution altering the results. As Obrimos historian, she is curious how Hallows can develop in to the same star clusters now and again \u2013 and she wants to see what, in reality, is King in Yellow.<br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> 5<br /> <b>Arcana:</b> Fate 2, Forces 4, Prime 3, Space 3, Time 5<br /> <br /> <b>I</b><b>phis - </b>Thyrsus of Free Council, 30-something white transvestite fringe evolutionist. He likes to walk as women for a few hours a day, but most of time he still thinks himself as more male persona \u2013 rather fluid, in the end. He believes that genders are mutation that was now planned from our Creators - First Ones made humanity as genderless, just like modern UFO myths describes \u201c<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey_alien\" target=\"_blank\">Grays</a>\u201d. He want to found where this happened, exactly, to try to revert this \u2013 at least for those that feel alien in their bodies. He spoke with some Planetary Spirits of Solar System and they sound to concur his theories. Yellow Sign, to him, could be validation of those theories and key to final understanding.<br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> 4<br /> <b>Arcana:</b> Life 5, Mind 2, Spirit 4, Time 4","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-02-2016, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T08:04:27-07:00","id":980243,"title":"","content":"You have Masters in there. They can cast single arcana Unmaking spells to instantly kill their opponents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T09:05:49-07:00","id":980270,"title":"","content":"Instant kills will instant kill my players PCs, so it's not very favorable outcome...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T09:37:37-07:00","id":980297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980165-\u200b-2e-fight-fire-with-fire-running-awakened-antagonists?p=980270#post980270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instant kills will instant kill my players PCs, so it's not very favorable outcome...</div> </div> </div> </div>So is there any reason that these Master level mages <i>wouldn't</i> just cast Unmaking spells at your players?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T09:38:49-07:00","id":980298,"title":"","content":"It is however challenging to be prepared for that kind of thing while still being well within the realm of something you can prepare for. I suggest showcasing it first by either snuffing out or nearly snuffing out an NPC so your players know the stakes before deciding if they want to continue the fight or come at their problem from some other angle. Another possibility is to have the NPCs in the group gain some intel that the PCs want to go up against Masters and they back out and refuse because no one wants to die instantly. There are a -lot- of ways to handle it so that the players will realize they're up against something really dangerous that could kill them all horrifically and the challenge is being prepared enough to come out alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 10-02-2016, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T09:45:44-07:00","id":980306,"title":"","content":"Combine Chaos Mastery (Fate 4) with Dispel Magic (Prime 1 with Fate 1) and cast it as an Area spell. Everyone except the Scelesti Cabal will suffer from environmental attacks. If they take time to prepare their Sanctum, &quot;Home Alone&quot; style, a lot can go wrong for the PCs. As a bonus, everything might accidentally catch fire.<br /> <br /> Wards and Signs (Prime 2) cast as an Area spell can disable most magic, forcing everyone to rely on non-Supernal magic, Attainments, ephemeral allies and ordinary weapons. They can also cast Praxes hoping for an Exceptional Success. The Scelesti might designate zones where magic works normally, so they can target the intruders and heal themselves. PCs need to figure out which places to occupy and which to avoid.<br /> <br /> Ephemeral Enchantment (Prime 3) can enchant knives to be usable by Spirits in Twilight. PCs get to be attacked by enemies they can't touch normally. Forge Purpose (Prime 5) can inspire a friendly NPC to follow the Scelesti agenda, but the effects are hard to predict. Eidolons (Prime 5) can sow chaos by impersonating either the Scelesti or the PCs.<br /> <br /> Innocuous objects, such as doorknobs, can be enchanted to release spells on touch.<br /> <br /> And that's just Prime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T23:44:36-07:00","id":980607,"title":"","content":"Do the Scelesti know that they're facing an imminent attack? Are the PCs/associated NPCs employing Time wards or similar measures to avoid being picked up by Prophecy or Divination from any of these Time 4-5 people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T00:02:59-07:00","id":980616,"title":"","content":"Well, Scelesti are all Time mages by Legacy, so I assume they Prophesied their attack, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T01:09:27-07:00","id":980643,"title":"","content":"That's a reasonable assumption if the PCs aren't running Shield of Chronos, yes... although looking over the antagonists' stats again, the odds of them failing the Clash of Wills seem pretty remote unless the attackers are also Gnosis 7 Time Masters. So, OK, the Scelesti will know the attack is coming, and will probably know the plan and the capabilities of those involved in detail. So, given that - what sort of capabilities are we talking about at the PC end? Is there a reason why the Scelesti are waiting to get hit rather than taking the initiative themselves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T02:45:21-07:00","id":980676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>General Tacticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980165-\u200b-2e-fight-fire-with-fire-running-awakened-antagonists?p=980643#post980643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, given that - what sort of capabilities are we talking about at the PC end? Is there a reason why the Scelesti are waiting to get hit rather than taking the initiative themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cabal of 4 Double Adepts or Masters of Arcana are PCs. As to reason to Scelesti - I did not think about that. I thought they reason they think rest of Concilium will sooner or later come to them, or hunt them, so hiding or running does not have sense. They want to pollute Observatory with Abyssal Magic and if they will have luck, they will run from it. At least Patterson can make Time Jump into future so she would omit all the Consilium backslash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T03:05:43-07:00","id":980682,"title":"","content":"One reason could be that they want to summon this Abyssal being, but they don't want to be the only potential targets of its (possibly) hostile attention when it arrives. Easier to get it to attack the &quot;weaker&quot; group and make their getaway.<br /> <br /> It serves another purpose too if the fight goes down in the observatory and that's where the Abyssal is summoned then it also pollutes the observatory with the Abyss. Two birds one stone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T04:34:09-07:00","id":980704,"title":"","content":"What sort of self-defence measures have the PCs been taking? Do they have Space or Time wards? Guardian spirits? Anything of that nature? If not, then if the Scelesti know they're coming, it seems more logical to me that they would take the offensive, allowing them to pick off some of their pending assailants individually and with surprise rather than letting them prepare and work together. If they have any source of Sympathy against the PCs, then Hastur's Space 4 should be particularly brutal; he can reach out and Sympathetically teleport people to, say, the bottom of the ocean, from the comfort of his living room, unless I am substantially misreading how Reach and spell factors work*.<br /> <br /> *Teleportation, +1 Reach for sensory range, +2 Reach for both ends being at sympathetic range, 1 Mana for the Sympathetic Range Attainment = 2 Paradox dice and 1 Mana to do this from anywhere in the world, without any resistance roll allowed on the part of the victim. 3 Paradox dice, if he wants to do it as an instant action. Even with a Weak sympathetic connection and not knowing the target's name, that's only Withstand 4; with a base Potency of 4 from his Arcana dots, he only needs to take a -2 on his casting roll for extra Potency. Which is so ridiculous that I feel like I <i>have</i> to be reading it wrong somehow, but I can't see how.<br /> <br /> Other options...<br /> <br /> Everyone who has Shifting Sands can use it to jump back a scene or more if something goes wrong with their plan, and get a do-over. For extra safety, someone can be waiting around with a few Hung Shifting Sands, watching the battle without participating (and thus without being in danger), and rewinding if things go against their buddies.<br /> <br /> Precession can entangle groups of enemies with Shared Fate, such that any damage or Conditions inflicted on one also affect the rest of the group. Combine with AoE effects or multi-target spells for hilarity. She can also spell up herself and her fellow Scelesti with a high-Potency casting of Wards and Signs to make them nigh-impervious to direct castings of hostile magic; doesn't do much again AoE boomspells, but many Arcana aren't really capable of those. <br /> <br /> Hastur can use Psychic Domination with the +2 Reach option to command enemy mages to commit suicide or kill one another. In fact, with another Reach spent for Advanced Scale, he can target all ten attacking mages simultaneously at only a -2 penalty (leaving him with 7 dice in his pool, before Yantras), and with a base Potency of 4. If he's worried about anyone Withstanding that with crazy Resolve, he can always add another level or two of Potency, he'll still be rolling 3-5 dice (plus Yantras and Willpower). He can also use Temporal Stutter with a Space 2 component to blink targetted enemies out of the fight and bring them back somewhere else, somewhere horribly inconvenient, like the aforementioned bottom of the ocean.<br /> <br /> Patterson can use Hung Spell to queue up a bunch of high-Potency Forces boom-spells, with Warding Gesture on her buddies to exclude them from the effects.<br /> <br /> Iphis can collect some potent Spirit minions and use Shape Spirit to alter them to the cabal's needs (e.g. change their Bans to &quot;must faithfully obey orders given by Iphis&quot;). He can also use Life 5 to create all manner of bizarre new life-forms to serve him, but I'm not sure how that works mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T05:04:15-07:00","id":980707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>General Tacticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980165-\u200b-2e-fight-fire-with-fire-running-awakened-antagonists?p=980704#post980704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What sort of self-defence measures have the PCs been taking? Do they have Space or Time wards? Guardian spirits? Anything of that nature? If not, then if the Scelesti know they're coming, it seems more logical to me that they would take the offensive, allowing them to pick off some of their pending assailants individually and with surprise rather than letting them prepare and work together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Easier would be to pick up PCs when they are outside of their or communal Sanctums, as those have high anti-magics countermeasures. Better is just to pick out PCs when they are on streets or on route.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>General Tacticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980165-\u200b-2e-fight-fire-with-fire-running-awakened-antagonists?p=980704#post980704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they have any source of Sympathy against the PCs, then Hastur's Space 4 should be particularly brutal; he can reach out and Sympathetically teleport people to, say, the bottom of the ocean, from the comfort of his living room, unless I am substantially misreading how Reach and spell factors work*.<br /> <br /> *Teleportation, +1 Reach for sensory range, +2 Reach for both ends being at sympathetic range, 1 Mana for the Sympathetic Range Attainment = 2 Paradox dice and 1 Mana to do this from anywhere in the world, without any resistance roll allowed on the part of the victim. 3 Paradox dice, if he wants to do it as an instant action. Even with a Weak sympathetic connection and not knowing the target's name, that's only Withstand 4; with a base Potency of 4 from his Arcana dots, he only needs to take a -2 on his casting roll for extra Potency. Which is so ridiculous that I feel like I <i>have</i> to be reading it wrong somehow, but I can't see how.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this is true... And remeber, Scelesti do not need to restict themeselves with Paradox Dices - they <i>want</i> to summon Abyss on this fight, to blight Observatory as gateway to their Madness God Realm. So more Reach Options used = More Paradox Dices = More 'bad' effects for Scelesti to use. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>General Tacticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980165-\u200b-2e-fight-fire-with-fire-running-awakened-antagonists?p=980704#post980704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone who has Shifting Sands can use it to jump back a scene or more if something goes wrong with their plan, and get a do-over. For extra safety, someone can be waiting around with a few Hung Shifting Sands, watching the battle without participating (and thus without being in danger), and rewinding if things go against their buddies.</div> </div> </div> </div>So we have answer on the Pattersons actions - we <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=920221#post920221\">house ruled Shifting Sands to work only few turns safetly</a>, but if she can play with open Paradox, she can create more than enough of those by repeating Shifitngs Sands. Looks like I can prepear my dead Cultist of Doomsday Clock to return to game with enough Temporal Paradox... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>General Tacticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980165-\u200b-2e-fight-fire-with-fire-running-awakened-antagonists?p=980704#post980704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iphis can collect some potent Spirit minions and use Shape Spirit to alter them to the cabal's needs (e.g. change their Bans to &quot;must faithfully obey orders given by Iphis&quot;). He can also use Life 5 to create all manner of bizarre new life-forms to serve him, but I'm not sure how that works mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Iphis, I was planing for him to cast Contagion from Life 5 to really kick characters in the ass, putting on them really long-killing disease.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T05:19:59-07:00","id":980709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980165-\u200b-2e-fight-fire-with-fire-running-awakened-antagonists?p=980707#post980707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Easier would be to pick up PCs when they are outside of their or communal Sanctums, as those have high anti-magics countermeasures. Better is just to pick out PCs when they are on streets or on route.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking while they were asleep, for maximal surprise, but if they have wards on where they sleep, then yeah, scry-and-fry while they're out shopping for groceries or whatever is probably the best bet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If this is true... And remeber, Scelesti do not need to restict themeselves with Paradox Dices - they <i>want</i> to summon Abyss on this fight, to blight Observatory as gateway to their Madness God Realm. So more Reach Options used = More Paradox Dices = More 'bad' effects for Scelesti to use. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Yup. If anything, the problem is that there aren't <i>enough</i> things to spend Reach on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So we have answer on the Pattersons actions - we <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=920221#post920221\">house ruled Shifting Sands to work only few turns safetly</a>, but if she can play with open Paradox, she can create more than enough of those by repeating Shifitngs Sands. Looks like I can prepear my dead Cultist of Doomsday Clock to return to game with enough Temporal Paradox... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense. TBH, I feel like 2e went seriously overboard with the time travel options available to Time mages. But it was an option available by RAW, so I reported it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For Iphis, I was planing for him to cast Contagion from Life 5 to really kick characters in the ass, putting on them really long-killing disease. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, infecting them with a modified Ebola strain or whatever would be a really nasty thing to do... but even the nastiest disease takes days to kill, which limits its effectiveness as a combat tactic, which is what I was focusing on.<br /> <br /> Oh, also, don't forget - anyone with Fate 2 or more can cast Exceptional Luck with the +2 Reach option to buff spellcasting, and can grant a +Potency bonus to Potency rolls. Just in case anyone's dice pools for casting horrifying LOLDEATH spells were feeling a bit low.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T08:16:14-07:00","id":980779,"title":"","content":"Also of note, for all the Scelesti - &quot;Present as Past&quot;, Time 4, guarantees the caster perfect information about all of the subjects' planned actions for the turn, and allows them to act themselves at the optimal time to mess up those plans. The effects of having everyone cast it can be more-or-less duplicated by having everyone use Acceleration and one person cast PaP, with Hastur of Iphis using a group-wide casting of Telepathy so that the PaP caster can pass their information to the rest of the group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T15:30:03-07:00","id":981071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980165-\u200b-2e-fight-fire-with-fire-running-awakened-antagonists?p=980270#post980270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instant kills will instant kill my players PCs, so it's not very favorable outcome...</div> </div> </div> </div>If Mages aren't anticipating death spells from other mages (unless you house rule them out - and even then, your players have to assume they're going to be throwing tons of aggravated damage) then they're doing it wrong. You shouldn't be getting into knock-down fights with other mages anyway, that's strictly a last resort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T17:09:45-07:00","id":981114,"title":"","content":"Simple solution: Gather everyone you can with as many dots in Forces as you can muster and level the Greenwich Observatory. &quot;Gas explosion&quot;.<br /> <br /> Honestly, there's no way an open confrontation ends well here. Your PCs could probably win by sheer numbers alone, but somebody's not going home. Unless there's a pressing need, give them space and wait them out. Wait for a moment of weakness and strike <i>then</i>, not while they're strong and focused. And if you can't wait for one, force one. Cast a spell turning all the water in the building into alkahest and turn on the sprinklers, say. Either they run or they melt. Force them off their home turf.<br /> <br /> But whatever you do, don't charge in and expect to come out without scars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T02:09:47-07:00","id":981354,"title":"","content":"There's a reason why open war between Mages is a rare event. Mutually Assured Destruction is a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T03:54:54-07:00","id":981378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980165-\u200b-2e-fight-fire-with-fire-running-awakened-antagonists?p=981071#post981071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Mages aren't anticipating death spells from other mages (unless you house rule them out - and even then, your players have to assume they're going to be throwing tons of aggravated damage) then they're doing it wrong. You shouldn't be getting into knock-down fights with other mages anyway, that's strictly a last resort.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. If your PCs are complaining about antagonist mages not acting like they would expect, and you're not having them attempt instant-kill spells as masters, or flinging around agg like there's no tomorrow (because there might not be if they don't), then that's likely the sole source of your problem.<br /> <br /> Like mentioned above - mutually assured destruction, or make damn sure you have a way to counter that kind of magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T11:40:47-07:00","id":981569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980165-\u200b-2e-fight-fire-with-fire-running-awakened-antagonists?p=981378#post981378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This. If your PCs are complaining about antagonist mages not acting like they would expect, and you're not having them attempt instant-kill spells as masters, or flinging around agg like there's no tomorrow (because there might not be if they don't), then that's likely the sole source of your problem.<br /> <br /> Like mentioned above - mutually assured destruction, or make damn sure you have a way to counter that kind of magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>On a slightly different note, I've contemplated what a game would look like if mages of the same effective level were largely immune to direct spells, in order to force more of a Sorcerer's Duel universe where powerful mages had to transform, alter the environment, and actually battle to hurt one another.<br /> <br /> Not something I think I'll implement, but it's kind of a neat idea now that I've had it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T11:57:07-07:00","id":981583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980165-\u200b-2e-fight-fire-with-fire-running-awakened-antagonists?p=981569#post981569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a slightly different note, I've contemplated what a game would look like if mages of the same effective level were largely immune to direct spells, in order to force more of a Sorcerer's Duel universe where powerful mages had to transform, alter the environment, and actually battle to hurt one another.<br /> <br /> Not something I think I'll implement, but it's kind of a neat idea now that I've had it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an interesting idea.<br /> <br /> It still allows for indirect methods of killing, which mages should be able to manage at that point.<br /> <br /> Instant-killing other mages seems like the type of thing that would offer some social stigma. Even if it was justified someone might think it was too much. But when you're dealing with something like wyrdhamsters crew of scelestus who aren't going to care, they have no reason not to hold back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}